  "problem": "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\n- $[4,8]\\cup [10,12]$\n- $[0,5)$\n- $[1,3)\\cup (3,7]$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[4,8]\\cup [10,12]$ is closed. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $4,8,10,$ and $12.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $[0,5)$ has a boundary point $5$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $[1,3)\\cup (3,7]$ has a boundary point $3$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
